      "content": "that's interesting. so you're saying the \"moral win\" of the R2P principle doesn't really hold up if the actual outcome is just more instability and extremism? it feels like the libs/internationalists always push for these interventions for moral reasons, but they rarely account for the actual geopolitical cost. do u think there's a way to actually balance morality and national interest, or is the \"intervening for human rights\" approach just fundamentally flawed?",
